---
import Page from "../layouts/Page.astro";
const updated = "October 30, 2026";
---
<Page
  title="Privacy | Even Butter Bake Shop"
  description="What Even Butter Bake Shop collects when you join the list, why, and how to get removed."
>
  <h1>Privacy</h1>
  <p><em>Last updated {updated}</em></p>
  <p>
    Even Butter Bake Shop is a small home bakery in North Miami, Florida. This page explains
    what we collect on this website and what we do with it. The short version: just your
    name and email, only to tell you when orders open.
  </p>

  <h2>What we collect</h2>
  <p>
    When you join the list, we save the name and email address you type in, plus the time
    you signed up. That's it. There are no accounts, no payments, and no tracking or
    advertising cookies on this site.
  </p>

  <h2>Why</h2>
  <p>
    To email you when orders open and to share bakery news, like new flavors and delivery
    details. We don't sell, rent, or share your information with anyone for their own
    marketing.
  </p>

  <h2>Where it's stored</h2>
  <p>
    Signups are stored in a database hosted by Supabase, a service provider that keeps the
    data on our behalf. Only the bakery can read the list.
  </p>
  <p>
    This site is hosted on GitHub Pages, and its fonts load from Google Fonts. Like any web
    host, those services may see your IP address and browser details when the page loads.
  </p>

  <h2>Getting removed</h2>
  <p>
    Every email from us includes a way to unsubscribe. You can also reply to any of our
    emails and ask us to delete your details, and we will.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    If this policy changes, we'll update this page and the date at the top.
  </p>
</Page>
